<h2>One section, three different routes</h2>
<p>Section 19 looks short but does three jobs at once. It creates the appeal, it excludes certain orders from appeal, and it preserves a revision for the maintenance jurisdiction the Family Courts exercise. Choosing the wrong route is not a technicality — an appeal filed where only a revision lies, or vice versa, costs weeks at the Registry and can imperil limitation.</p>
<table class="law">
  <tr><th>What the Family Court decided</th><th>The route out</th><th>Forum</th></tr>
